            <ArticleTitle>Multiple action compounds in angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Carvedilol--a vasodilating beta-blocker has been shown in multicentre trials to be as effective as standard beta-blockers in improving exercise tolerance in patients with angina pectoris and it is more effective than nifedipine. The side effects are less than conventional beta-blockers and nifedipine. Carvedilol is an effective anti-anginal therapy and improves the quality of life.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
